data: {"item_id":"rs_642883","output_index":0,"sequence_number":149,"summary_index":0,"text":"We need to fix previous submission errors. The feedback indicates that a tool call to apply_patch had invalid JSON due to quoting etc. Also git status shows modifications not committed. We need to apply a proper patch via exec_command. We'll need to edit files accordingly, ensure all requirements are met for Task 002 (including Task 001). Likely the repository already has some code but with errors. We need to run git status to see repo state, then apply patches, run tests? There is no test harness given but we can run npm start maybe to ensure health endpoint works. But we need to commit changes, and then report commit ID. So steps: check repo files, status, maybe run lint? We'll inspect repository.","type":"response.reasoning_summary_text.done"}

